Dark areas mean (especially for non-infravision races) that
a) You cannot see what's approaching; in case one monster
(or in the open mine area even a horde of monsters) aim at
you you'll notice that just at the moment they are adjacent
(or have thrown some missile at you); you will then have to
select from a _much_ smaller set of possible counteractions.
b) You generally have to inspect a lot more dungeon squares
thus increasing the probability of hitting a trap; you have
surely noticed that any traps will reduce your character's
live expectations significantly (magic trap creates monsters,
trapdoor separates you from your pet, pits and bear traps
reduce your mobility, e.g. to flee, and even stone traps
will, for a PR player, be a risk because of the reduction
of the already only few HPs).
c) Monsters can take advantage of the interesting items that
are lying around before you see them (defensive items like
potions of healing, of offensive items like wands).
